	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type `cv` in Alfred to edit the current clipboard contents in nvim.

Flow: in pi, ctrl+x copies the last agent message. Type `cv` in Alfred. A fresh
lightweight Ghostty window opens nvim (with your config + line numbers) on the
clipboard text. Edit it, then:
  :wq  -> the edited buffer is copied back to the clipboard (notification confirms)
  :cq  -> abort, clipboard left untouched

The script lives in the dotfiles repo at ~/.scripts/cv (versioned), not inside
this workflow, so it is maintained alongside the rest of Ben's tooling.</string>
